    "primary_module": "lightning.pytorch.callbacks.timer",
    "prompt": "The `Timer` callback in `lightning.pytorch.callbacks.timer` has a bug: when `duration` is expressed as a `timedelta`, it is compared against wall-clock seconds as if it were already a float, causing premature training stops on long runs.\n\nBefore touching the module, map the blast radius:\n1. Which modules directly import `lightning.pytorch.callbacks.timer`? List every one by full dotted name.\n2. For each direct importer, state how many other modules import it in turn \u2014 this is the second-order exposure.\n3. Identify the single importer with the highest second-order exposure; it carries the most amplified risk.\n\nProduce the direct-importer list with second-order counts and name the top-risk importer. Do not implement the fix.",
    "prompt_sha256": "6f184b152622b43506fc561cbc080a0fbc8093c1b475c7c3664f26a0be086479",
